    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for high-upside production today, led by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Kyle Tucker** (71.28). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is our premier start, capitalizing on a soft matchup against Pecko (xERA 5.95) and a favorable #3 hole, providing the highest ceiling for volume and efficiency. **Kyle Tucker** follows closely, benefiting from a positive park factor and a comfortable matchup against Elder. Additionally, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.26) remains a set-and-forget anchor, as he continues to thrive against Lugo despite a slight platoon dip. These three represent the core of our offensive engine, each carrying the momentum required to capitalize on high-xERA starters.\n\nStrategic platoon adjustments define the middle of our lineup, where we are leaning heavily into favorable splits to maintain our competitive edge. **Liam Hicks** (55.40) receives a significant 11% boost from his dynamic platoon advantage against Jobe, while **Luis Robert Jr.** (52.66) and **Gunnar Henderson** (53.04) are deployed to exploit matchup variances, even as **Gunnar Henderson** faces a tougher tactical look against Liberatore. **Sam Antonacci** and **Drake Baldwin** are forced into lower scores due to their daunting matchups against deGrom and Glasnow, respectively, though both retain start-worthy status based on their premium batting order slots.\n\nThe primary tension in today\u2019s selection was the exclusion of **Miguel Vargas** (39.60), who narrowly missed the starting cut by failing to clear our 40.0 floor. While his xwOBA remains strong, the combination of facing an elite arm in deGrom and the lack of a sufficient situational advantage made him the clear odd man out. Investors should remain vigilant regarding **Jackson Merrill**, whose 49.47 score is contingent on his anticipated #5 slot in the order; with the lineup pending and an elite matchup against Skenes, his projection remains volatile. We continue to monitor the status of our sidelined core, including **Jordan Westburg**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jacob Wilson**, whose continued absence on the IL underscores the importance of the production we are currently squeezing out of our active bench options like **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, and **Tommy White**.",
